 "name": "Farm Plot Size and Landscape Beauty",
 "description": "Faithful replication of the landscape rating task in Janeckova Molnarova, Bohnet, Svobodova, Černý Pixová, Daniels, Skaloš, Drhlíková, Azadi, Zámečník & Sklenička (2023), \"Does Increasing Farm Plot Size Influence the Visual Quality of Everyday Agricultural Landscapes?\", International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health 20(1):687, doi:10.3390/ijerph20010687. Participants see the same Czech farmland views with the fields split in Photoshop into plots of about 50, 35, 20, 10 or 5 ha, in random order, and rate each from 1 = very ugly to 7 = very beautiful; then gender, age group, education, size of birth and current municipality, and occupation group. Original sample: 1,033 Czech adults (2016). Images are the authors' photomontages from Figure 2 of the open-access paper (CC BY 4.0), used with credit; the template is taken down if the authors object. Differences from the original study: (1) only landscapes A (flat, almost no woody vegetation) and D (varied relief, dense woody vegetation) are included, because the B and C series were not published; each original respondent rated two of the four series; (2) the seven unmanipulated control photographs were not published and are left out; (3) the images are cut from the published figure (about 590 × 310 px) and the A1–D5 labels were digitally removed; (4) municipality of birth and residence are asked directly as five size categories, and the 14 Czech regions are left out.",
